This is the testing framework for use in Iowa's DUNE DC to DC Converter Box assembly, in a nearly complete state.
All files are required for proper execution, but only MainTesting must be run. In order to assure database consistency,
please ensure that each board ID is consistent across both temperature sets (CASE SENSITIVE). User will initially be
prompted to input their name and select a testing phase. Ask Niko if needed phase is missing or other imputation error
occurs.

Configuration is done in Config.py, the procedure will typically prompt you when edits are needed.

FetchBoardData will give you a list of all boards and their results on an Excel Sheet, and can also be used to retrieve
the scope trace data of any board. User must change destination paths or data will fail to download. The trace lengths
are Input Voltage Trace 3000ms, Nominal Load Trace 2000ms, Input Step Voltage Trace 2000ms, Output Step Trace 2000ms,
and Cold Startup Trace 5000ms. Power cycle tests are done over 5 cycles with 20 measurements of current and voltage
each. Unfortunately, as of now there is no feasible way to write and read from two channels at once, so each test which
requires both a current and voltage trace is performed twice; planning to patch this later.

For now, all the tests that need be done are contained in MainTesting.

PS. If the timer sounds annoy you, there is a config option to silence them :)


================================================= PHASE DESCRIPTIONS ===================================================


Non-Shielded: Early testing generic phase which consists of unmodified, unshielded boards which do no necessarily have
              the diode replacement.

New Diodes: Same parameters as above, but requiring the diodes have been replaced with new ones.
